<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Papeete</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Papeete is the capital of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a>, on the north-west coast of Tahiti. It grew around a harbour used by whalers and traders in the early 19th century and became the seat of the Pōmare monarchy and then of the French administration after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> of 1842. It is the territory's main port, and its international airport lies in neighbouring Faaa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/papeete.jpg" alt="Papeete" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Remi Jouan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Papeete_-_Marina_Taina.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
